15 0 obj
<<
/A 39 0 R
/Alt (Flowchart illustrating rhinitis medicamentosa. It shows two pathways: a healthy state and a diseased state. The healthy state involves correct use of nasal vasoconstrictors leading to norepinephrine release, activating adrenergic receptors, resulting in vasoconstriction and vasodilation. The diseased state involves prolonged use of nasal vasoconstrictors causing nerve degeneration, reduced norepinephrine release, and rebound congestion, activating adrenergic receptors and causing vasodilation or reduced vasoconstriction. The process leads to rebound congestion.)
/K 0
/P 7 0 R
/Pg 29 0 R
/S /Figure
/T (Figure)
>>
endobj
16 0 obj
<<
/A 39 0 R
/Alt (Flowchart depicting a cycle beginning with "Prolonged use of nasal decongestant" leading to "Reduced mucociliary clearance" and "Inflammatory mediators persist at nasal mucosa." This continues to "Continued inflammation," causing "Continued nasal swelling" and "Damage to nasal epithelia." The cycle progresses to "Cell death," then "Tissue exposed to PAMPs," leading to "Leukocyte and neutrophil infiltration," which loops back to "Inflammatory mediators persist at nasal mucosa.")
/K 0
/P 7 0 R
/Pg 30 0 R
/S /Figure
/T (Figure)
>>
endobj
17 0 obj
<<
/A 39 0 R
/Alt (Flowchart illustrating nasal congestion treatment. It starts with a patient suffering from congestion. If enough time has elapsed since the last dose, they use nasal spray. Congestion eases, but effects wear off. If treatment hasn't been used for the maximum time, it repeats. Otherwise, the patient should stop using the decongestant. Misuse, reliance, or ignoring recommended time can cause rebound congestion. Effects diminish if no further treatment is used.)
/K 0
/P 7 0 R
/Pg 33 0 R
/S /Figure
/T (Figure)
>>
endobj
18 0 obj
<<
/A 39 0 R
/Alt (Flowchart describing treatment for rhinitis medicamentosa. Step 1: Diagnose and implement reduced dosage, intranasal steroids, patient education, and saline washes. If necessary, add oral steroids. Step 2: Consider nebulised hyaluronic acid or UV endonasal phototherapy. Step 3: Nasal surgery.)
/K 0
/P 7 0 R
/Pg 35 0 R
/S /Figure
/T (Figure)
>>
endobj
